This study introduces a multi-dimensional, diverse, and extensive dataset called Beijing socioeconomic dataset, which is designed to facilitate the analysis of socioeconomic research in the city. Comprising a wide range of attributes including economic, educational, transportation, and healthcare systems, this dataset empowers researchers to explore various research interests. Comprising over 210 million records and covering over 1500 neighborhoods, this dataset is characterized by its massive size, diverse sources, and multiple data types. Utilizing several evaluation methods, our study confirms that this dataset is free from bias as evidenced by the correlation between various natural language key performance indicators and actual socioeconomic levels. A thorough assessment of the dataset is conducted through multiple statistical tests, which reveal its internal consistency and quality integrity. A call for research is issued, accompanied by relevant data, code, and documentation which are publicly available on GitHub. Furthermore, this study is accompanied by a special issue in Information Systems frontiers focusing on the topic "Advances in Modern Dataset with Diversity in Geographic Information" with an associated call for papers. 

